    "notes": "Proportions taken from the NOAA Fisheries species illustration (snout tip to caudal base = SL): short, deep, strongly compressed apogonid body, bony torso SL/BH about 1.95 (illustration 2.06, Ndobe et al. 2013 2.07; width about 0.38 of depth), the visible silhouette including the broad pelvic lobe about 1.2 SL/height. Straight steep forehead (about 33 degrees) from a short blunt snout to the nape at the first-dorsal origin, deep abrupt chest, belly nearly flat to the anal origin, depth carried back to the second-dorsal origin, then a quick taper to a short thick peduncle (16% SL deep, 12% SL long). Large head (HL 35% SL) with a big lateral eye (12.4% SL) seated in the head bar at 15% SL behind the tip and a broad oblique terminal mouth. Fins: first dorsal a tall black sail (31% SL) with backward-bowed hooked leading spines; second dorsal a thick black anterior ray running out as a bowed filament (74% SL along the ray) with a large pale swept sail (21% SL tall) behind it; anal a broad tapering black lobe (41% SL) with a pale sail behind it; pelvic a broad rounded black spotted lobe (38% SL) hanging under the anterior belly; clear pectorals; caudal with long black upper and lower bands (45% SL) framing a pale deeply forked centre.",
