  "visualDebt": [
    "First-dorsal spines are one bowed thin shell whose leading membrane is painted pale and dissolved between the spines; the hook is a smooth quadratic bow, not a sharp crook.",
    "Second-dorsal filament and anal lobe are separate bowed thin shells abutting their pale sails at the base; the join is a shared base edge, not a continuous membrane.",
    "White spot pattern is procedural and identical across builds; real individuals carry unique spot patterns.",
    "Mouth is the shared plan's tube lip cue on a blunt snout plus a painted oblique gape cleft; the large gape (MG 27% SL) is not modelled as an opening.",
    "Reference silhouette measured on the NOAA illustration; live fish vary in fin-ray length and bar width."
  ]
